Stacked on #<parent> (`bodhi/questionnaire-actions`). Adapts the Claude Design "Questionnaire Builder" reference UI into a 3-pane WYSIWYG builder whose canvas is rendered by a new full renderer, built separately from the existing rendering shells so they can be removed cleanly after review.

## What this adds

### `form/` — the full renderer (`QuestionnaireFormRenderer`)
The whole questionnaire on one scroll: top-level groups as section cards, plain questions as standalone cards. Built as a second consumer of the existing renderer **engine** (`renderer/store.ts` with the frozen `evaluateEnableWhen` port, `renderer/inputs/*`, the type/structured registries, the styling sanitizer) — none of those files change. Everything shell-shaped is new:

- **Live sync**: the provider merges responses on every questions-tree change (keep by id when type/structured_type/options unchanged, seed added, drop removed) instead of the old wipe-on-reseed — a builder can feed it a fresh draft per keystroke and in-progress preview answers survive.
- **Decoration seam**: an optional `QuestionShell`/`AppendZone` chrome context lets a host wrap every block (selection ring, toolbar) without the renderer knowing the builder exists.
- **`revealHidden`/`inert`** flags for the edit canvas: logic-hidden questions render with a badge; inputs stay visible but leave the a11y tree and pass clicks to the chrome.
- **Structured questions** reuse the existing QuestionTypes UI through the registry adapter, with the requires-context placeholder in builder scope, a memoized update callback (ChargeItemQuestion effect-loop hazard), and fill-mode `questionnaireId`/`slug` pass-through.
- **Fill seams**: mode union includes `fill`, `validation.ts` implements the `errorsAtom` writer the old renderer documented. The encounter fill host + batch submission are the next stacked PR.
- `data-question-id` is stamped on every block — hosts scroll to it and specs scope with it.

### `studio/` — the 3-pane builder (replaces the old builder page on both `/edit` mounts)
- **Top bar**: back, title + revision chip + status badge, a save-blocking **issues popover** (every failing rule, click-to-fix) / "Ready to save", the Edit/Preview toggle, **Discard** (resets draft + metadata from cache), Save Changes.
- **Left outline**: search (filters rows, numbering stable), a **Form settings** row, the single navigation tree with insert-`+` separators, Add question / Add section, the mobile Select fallback (+ mobile add button).
- **Canvas**: the live form renderer. Edit mode overlays selection chrome — ring, EDITING badge, floating move/duplicate/delete toolbar, per-section dashed add zones, hidden-by-logic badges. Preview mode is the plain interactive form with live enable_when; answers survive Edit↔Preview toggles and question edits.
- **Right inspector**: the existing `QuestionEditorCard` for questions/groups (type picker, options, unit rows, Behaviour/Visibility/Coding cards, sub-question tooling — all reused), and a Form settings panel composing the manage metadata pieces (title/slug/description/status via the shared zod schema, organizations, clone, JSON export of the current draft). Save is still **one full-body PUT** via `buildUpdateBody`, now carrying the metadata edits too.

Model-layer groundwork: `duplicateQuestion` reducer action (internal enable_when targets remap, external ones preserved), `template` on `addQuestion` (atomic Add section), `findInvalidQuestions` (all issues; `findFirstInvalidQuestion` is element 0 so save-toast order is unchanged), `downloadQuestionnaireJson` lifted to `shared/`.

## Deliberate adaptations from the reference
- Collapsible settings cards instead of the reference's Question/Logic/Coding tabs — same progressive disclosure, keeps the existing editor internals and their test contracts.
- Organizations instead of tags (no tags field on the backend model); status field instead of a Publish action (no publish endpoint — revisioning stays backend-side on save).
- The inspector precedes the canvas in DOM (visual order via flex `order-*`) so the type picker stays the first combobox on the editor surface; canvas inputs are `inert` in edit mode, so the canvas contributes no roles there.

## What stays untouched (removal after review)
- The old paginated renderer shell (`renderer/QuestionnaireRenderer` + pagination components) still powers the detail/revision pages.
- The old `builder/QuestionnaireBuilderPage` shell is in-tree but unmounted.
- The legacy fill flow (`src/components/Questionnaire`) is untouched.

